      "titleEn": "Practise with AI",
      "instructions": "Hãy viết 2-3 câu tiếng Anh dùng would: một điều bạn rất thích được làm (I'd love to ...), một việc bạn sẽ không muốn làm (I wouldn't like to ...), và một thói quen hồi nhỏ của bạn (When I was a child, I would ...).",
      "instructionsEn": "Write 2-3 English sentences using would: something you would love to do (I'd love to ...), something you would not like to do (I wouldn't like to ...), and a childhood habit (When I was a child, I would ...).",
      "ruleSummary": "This unit practises would. would ('d) and wouldn't introduce an imagined, unreal situation (It would be nice to buy a new car, but we can't afford it; I'd love to live by the sea), and would have + past participle imagines something that did not happen in the past (I don't know what we'd have done without their help; You would have liked it). Compare will, which is for what is really going to happen, with would, which signals that it is not (I'll stay a little longer versus I'd stay a little longer, but I have to go). would is also the past of will in reported speech (He said he'd call me), and wouldn't can mean refused to (I tried to warn him, but he wouldn't listen; The car wouldn't start). Finally would describes repeated actions in the past, much like used to (Whenever Richard was angry, he would walk out of the room). A correct student sentence must use would + base verb, or would have + past participle for an unreal past, and must not use would where the situation is real and expected."
